<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.17.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02054</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.17.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b2b0db0c-0c07-4980-aabb-0b6b12518b28</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="2252dcce-e1e0-4a08-b5c2-468676440321" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <newline/>
            <para>Here is the graph of quadratic function \(f\).</para>
            <para>Andre uses the expression \((x−5)^2+7\) to define \(f\).</para>
            <para>Noah uses the expression \((x+5)^2−7\) to define \(f\).</para>
            <para>Do you agree with either of them? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para> Correct! No. The vertex of the graph is (5,-7). The graph of Andre’s function would have a vertex at (5,7), and the graph of Noah’s function would have a vertex at (-5,-7).</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is No. The vertex of the graph is (5,-7). The graph of Andre’s function would have a vertex at (5,7), and the graph of Noah’s function would have a vertex at (-5,-7). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="282d6d0c-46f8-46a0-badc-fc34c38a8ccd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <newline/>
            <para>Here are the graphs of \(f(x)=x^2\), \(f(x)=x^2−5\), and \(f(x)=(x+2)^2−8\).</para>
            <para> How do the three graphs compare?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>They all have the same vertex.</para>
            <para>The shape is the same but they are in different locations.</para>
            <para>They all have a negative a coefficient in the vertex form of the equation. </para>
            <para>All three graphs contain the point \((0,0)\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The shape is the same but they are in different locations.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: The shape is the same but they are in different locations. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="44662707-e10a-4387-b777-c39c27a3d344" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> Compare the graphs of \(f(x)=x^2\) and \(f(x)=x^2−5\). What role does the -5 play in the comparison?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph left by 5 units.</para>
            <para>Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph right by 5 units.</para>
            <para>Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph up by 5 units.</para>
            <para>Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para> The correct answer is: Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="72dc86cb-6e3f-4c54-8a83-e694249dc1cd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para> Compare the graphs of \(f(x)=x^2\) and \(f(x)=(x+2)^2−8\). What roles do the \(+2\) and \(-8\) play in the comparison?</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>Adding 2 to \(x\) before squaring shifts the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units.</para>
            <para>Adding 2 to \(x\) before squaring shifts the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) to the up by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph left by 8 units.</para>
            <para>Adding 2 to \(x\) before squaring shifts the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) to the right by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph up by 8 units.</para>
            <para>Adding 2 to \(x\) before squaring shifts the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) to the down by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph right by 8 units.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Adding 2 to \(x\) before squaring shifts the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is: Adding 2 to \(x\) before squaring shifts the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="1f55aa1e-b16c-4b06-a84d-cc7775bce93f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para><emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> equations with a graph whose vertex has both a positive \(x\) and a positive \(y\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.17.2 – 7.17.5. </para>
            <para>The correct answers are: \(f(x)=(x−3)^2+2, f(x)=-(x−4)^2+3, f(x)=-2(x−3)^2+1\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="7667ebf6-4a0e-43ee-ad68-e4122e29fcd1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which equation represents the graph shown?
          
          <figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A DOWNWARD PARABOLA WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 7, 3"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_19_11_01.jpg"/></media></figure></para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=-(x+7)^2+3\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=-(x-7)^2+3\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=(x+7)^2+3\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x)=(x-7)^2+3\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para> Correct! \(f(x)=-(x+7)^2+3\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=-(x+7)^2+3\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="9a934902-5287-41e8-9605-420df0d5afb2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The graph representing \(f(x)=x^2\) is shifted 4 units to the left, 16 units down, and flipped so it opens downward (reflects over the \(x\)-axis). Which equation defines the curve?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(f(x)=-(x+4)^2-16\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=-(x+4)^2-16\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="98eb9153-ec2e-4bec-8e61-67ae884326f0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>The graph of \(f(x) = x^2\) is transformed by a horizontal dilation of \(\frac12\). What is the equation of the function that results from this translation? </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) =\frac 12 x^2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + \frac12\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = (x-\frac 12)^2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = (\frac12x)^2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para> Correct! \(f(x) = (\frac12x)^2\) </para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = (\frac12x)^2\) . </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e7ef5d3c-1203-48a7-bcbc-cc6e2525319c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Select the two descriptions that apply.</para>
            <para>A function \(g(x) = (2x)^2 - 5\) was transformed from the parent quadratic function. Which of the following answer choices describes the transformations that were applied? </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! A horizontal dilation by a factor of 2 and A vertical shift down 5 units </para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.17.2 – 7.17.5. </para>
            <para>The correct answer are: A horizontal dilation by a factor of 2 and A vertical shift down 5 units. </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="0a126082-3fce-4bb1-afd0-2bbcb81e7ef9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following represents a function that has experienced a horizontal compression? </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = (-1x)^2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = (\frac 15x)^2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = (\frac 52x)^2\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para> Correct! \(f(x) = (\frac 52x)^2\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = (\frac 52x)^2\) . </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
